name wordnet-cntlist
# cntlist.5: "The fields are separated by one space", and
#   "Each line in cntlist is of the form:   tag_cnt  sense_key  sense_number"
# The sense key is WordNet's key of the sense, read as the ILI concept it is mapped to; the sense number is where the
# sense stands in the lemma's list, a key; the tag count is what the file says of the sense.
match cntlist

tier row by \n
names tag_cnt sense_key sense_number
tier field by space

thing row sense_key
type sense_key ili
key row sense_number
content tag_cnt
# cntlist.5: "tag_cnt is the decimal number of times the sense is tagged in the corresponding semantic concordance": a
# number the file states of the sense, an observation. The sense key is read as the concept its synset is (type
# sense_key ili), so the claim is said of the concept, not of the lemma's sense: the sense key as the lexicalization
# [lemma, language, ILI] is Laplace-Engine#20.
relation "number of times the sense is tagged" tag_cnt
attest row tag_cnt
